'$VAR' was passed to a function after being freed. This can lead to undefined behavior."},"id":"AIK_c_sec_use-after-free_function","name":"AIK_c_sec_use-after-free_function","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_c_sec_use-after-free_function"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Avoid 'gets()'. This function does not consider buffer boundaries and can lead to buffer overflows. Use 'fgets()' or 'gets_s()' instead."},"help":{"markdown":"Avoid 'gets()'. This function does not consider buffer boundaries and can lead to buffer overflows. Use 'fgets()' or 'gets_s()' instead.","text":"Avoid 'gets()'. This function does not consider buffer boundaries and can lead to buffer overflows. Use 'fgets()' or 'gets_s()' instead."},"id":"AIK_c_sec_use-gets-fn","name":"AIK_c_sec_use-gets-fn","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_c_sec_use-gets-fn"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"format string attack detected"},"help":{"markdown":"format string attack detected","text":"format string attack detected"},"id":"AIK_c_sec_use-printf-fn","name":"AIK_c_sec_use-printf-fn","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_c_sec_use-printf-fn"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential for OS command injection."},"help":{"markdown":"Potential for OS command injection.","text":"Potential for OS command injection."},"id":"AIK_c_shell_execl_execlp","name":"AIK_c_shell_execl_execlp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_c_shell_execl_execlp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential for OS command injection."},"help":{"markdown":"Potential for OS command injection.","text":"Potential for OS command injection."},"id":"AIK_c_shell_system","name":"AIK_c_shell_system","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_c_shell_system"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Use of deprecated function (mktemp)."},"help":{"markdown":"Use of deprecated function (mktemp).","text":"Use of deprecated function (mktemp)."},"id":"AIK_c_tmpfile_mktemp","name":"AIK_c_tmpfile_mktemp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_c_tmpfile_mktemp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application uses CakePHP's native database functions with potential user input."},"help":{"markdown":"The application uses CakePHP's native database functions with potential user input.","text":"The application uses CakePHP's native database functions with potential user input."},"id":"AIK_cakephp-sql-injection","name":"AIK_cakephp-sql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_cakephp-sql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The default mass assignment protection configuration is overridden and set to 'True', which is discouraged as it may introduce mass assignment vulnerabilities."},"help":{"markdown":"The default mass assignment protection configuration is overridden and set to 'True', which is discouraged as it may introduce mass assignment vulnerabilities.","text":"The default mass assignment protection configuration is overridden and set to 'True', which is discouraged as it may introduce mass assignment vulnerabilities."},"id":"AIK_check-mass-assignment-config","name":"AIK_check-mass-assignment-config","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_check-mass-assignment-config"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"You are using the 'send' method on a Ruby object with user input, which allows an attacker to call any method on the object (incl. any defined Kernel methods), which leads to RCE."},"help":{"markdown":"You are using the 'send' method on a Ruby object with user input, which allows an attacker to call any method on the object (incl. any defined Kernel methods), which leads to RCE.","text":"You are using the 'send' method on a Ruby object with user input, which allows an attacker to call any method on the object (incl. any defined Kernel methods), which leads to RCE."},"id":"AIK_check-reflection-use","name":"AIK_check-reflection-use","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_check-reflection-use"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Unsigned JWT usage detected"},"help":{"markdown":"Unsigned JWT usage detected","text":"Unsigned JWT usage detected"},"id":"AIK_clojure-unsigned-jwt","name":"AIK_clojure-unsigned-jwt","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure-unsigned-jwt"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Do not call clojure.java.shell using potential user-controlled inputs as it may leads to RCE."},"help":{"markdown":"Do not call clojure.java.shell using potential user-controlled inputs as it may leads to RCE.","text":"Do not call clojure.java.shell using potential user-controlled inputs as it may leads to RCE."},"id":"AIK_clojure_command_injection","name":"AIK_clojure_command_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure_command_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"WARNING: You SHOULD NOT handle user-controlled inputs into code evaluation functions like clojure.core/eval or clojure.core/load-string."},"help":{"markdown":"WARNING: You SHOULD NOT handle user-controlled inputs into code evaluation functions like clojure.core/eval or clojure.core/load-string.","text":"WARNING: You SHOULD NOT handle user-controlled inputs into code evaluation functions like clojure.core/eval or clojure.core/load-string."},"id":"AIK_clojure_eval_injection","name":"AIK_clojure_eval_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure_eval_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"WARNING: You SHOULD NOT use clojure.core/read or clojure.core/read-string to read data from untrusted sources."},"help":{"markdown":"WARNING: You SHOULD NOT use clojure.core/read or clojure.core/read-string to read data from untrusted sources.","text":"WARNING: You SHOULD NOT use clojure.core/read or clojure.core/read-string to read data from untrusted sources."},"id":"AIK_clojure_insecure_deserialization_read","name":"AIK_clojure_insecure_deserialization_read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure_insecure_deserialization_read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Insecure protocol for SSL Context"},"help":{"markdown":"Insecure protocol for SSL Context","text":"Insecure protocol for SSL Context"},"id":"AIK_clojure_insecure_ssl_protocol","name":"AIK_clojure_insecure_ssl_protocol","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure_insecure_ssl_protocol"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential Path Traversal vulnerability detected, user input passed to file handling methods."},"help":{"markdown":"Potential Path Traversal vulnerability detected, user input passed to file handling methods.","text":"Potential Path Traversal vulnerability detected, user input passed to file handling methods."},"id":"AIK_clojure_path_traversal","name":"AIK_clojure_path_traversal","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure_path_traversal"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible SQL injection. Untrusted input $PARAM"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible SQL injection. Untrusted input $PARAM","text":"Possible SQL injection. Untrusted input $PARAM"},"id":"AIK_clojure_sqli","name":"AIK_clojure_sqli","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_clojure_sqli"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The input values included in SQL queries need to be passed in safely. Bind\nvariables in prepared statements can be used to easily mitigate the risk of\nSQL injection.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The input values included in SQL queries need to be passed in safely. Bind\nvariables in prepared statements can be used to easily mitigate the risk of\nSQL injection.\n","text":"The input values included in SQL queries need to be passed in safely. Bind\nvariables in prepared statements can be used to easily mitigate the risk of\nSQL injection.\n"},"id":"AIK_cpp_sqli","name":"AIK_cpp_sqli","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_cpp_sqli"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"strcpy found"},"help":{"markdown":"strcpy found","text":"strcpy found"},"id":"AIK_cpp_strcpy","name":"AIK_cpp_strcpy","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_cpp_strcpy"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cookie Security Misconfiguration Detected"},"help":{"markdown":"Cookie Security Misconfiguration Detected","text":"Cookie Security Misconfiguration Detected"},"id":"AIK_csharp-cookie-security","name":"AIK_csharp-cookie-security","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp-cookie-security"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Deprecated SSL Protocol Usage Detected"},"help":{"markdown":"Deprecated SSL Protocol Usage Detected","text":"Deprecated SSL Protocol Usage Detected"},"id":"AIK_csharp-deprecated-ssl-protocol-usage","name":"AIK_csharp-deprecated-ssl-protocol-usage","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp-deprecated-ssl-protocol-usage"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Improper Certificate Validation Detected"},"help":{"markdown":"Improper Certificate Validation Detected","text":"Improper Certificate Validation Detected"},"id":"AIK_csharp-disable-certificate-validation","name":"AIK_csharp-disable-certificate-validation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp-disable-certificate-validation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"OS command injection possible"},"help":{"markdown":"OS command injection possible","text":"OS command injection possible"},"id":"AIK_csharp_CommandInjection","name":"AIK_csharp_CommandInjection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_CommandInjection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a NoSQL injection vulnerability."},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a NoSQL injection vulnerability.","text":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a NoSQL injection vulnerability."},"id":"AIK_csharp_NoSQLInjection","name":"AIK_csharp_NoSQLInjection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_NoSQLInjection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a SQL injection vulnerability."},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a SQL injection vulnerability.","text":"Untrusted input might be used to build a database query, which can lead to a SQL injection vulnerability."},"id":"AIK_csharp_SQLInjection","name":"AIK_csharp_SQLInjection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_SQLInjection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Having the annotation [OutputCache] will disable the annotation [Authorize] for\nthe requests following the first one.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Having the annotation [OutputCache] will disable the annotation [Authorize] for\nthe requests following the first one.\n","text":"Having the annotation [OutputCache] will disable the annotation [Authorize] for\nthe requests following the first one.\n"},"id":"AIK_csharp_cache_OutputCacheConflicts","name":"AIK_csharp_cache_OutputCacheConflicts","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_cache_OutputCacheConflicts"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cryptographic algorithms provide many different modes of operation, only some of which provide\nmessage integrity. Without message integrity it could be possible for an adversary to attempt\nto tamper with the ciphertext which could lead to compromising the encryption key. Newer\nalgorithms\napply message integrity to validate ciphertext has not been tampered with.\n\nInstead of using an algorithm that requires configuring a `CipherMode`, an algorithm\nthat has built-in message integrity should be used. If using .NET Framework greater\nthan version 6.0 consider using `ChaCha20Poly1305` or `AES-256-GCM`.\n\nFor older applications, `AES-256-GCM` is recommended, however it has many drawbacks:\n- Slower than `ChaCha20Poly1305`.\n- Catastrophic failure if nonce values are re-used.\n\nExample using `ChaCha20Poly1305`:\n```\n// Generate a random key\nbyte[] key = new byte[32];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(key);\n\nChaCha20Poly1305 encryptor = new ChaCha20Poly1305(key);\n\n// Note nonce values _must_ be regenerated every time they are used.\nvar nonce = new byte[12];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(nonce);\n\nbyte[] plainText = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"Secret text to encrypt\");\nbyte[] cipherText = new byte[plainText.Length];\nvar authTag = new byte[16];\n\nencryptor.Encrypt(nonce, plainText, cipherText, authTag);\nbyte[] output = new byte[cipherText.Length];\nencryptor.Decrypt(nonce, cipherText, authTag, output);\nConsole.WriteLine(\"Output: {0}\", System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(output));\n```\n\nExample using `AES-256-GCM`:\n```\nvar plaintextBytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"Secret text to encrypt\");\nvar key = new byte[32];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(key);\n\nusing var aes = new AesGcm(key);\nvar nonce = new byte[AesGcm.NonceByteSizes.MaxSize];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(nonce);\n\nvar cipherText = new byte[plaintextBytes.Length];\nvar tag = new byte[AesGcm.TagByteSizes.MaxSize];\n\naes.Encrypt(nonce, plaintextBytes, cipherText, tag);\n\n// Decrypt\nusing (var decrypt = new AesGcm(key))\n{\n    var decryptedBytes = new byte[cipherText.Length];\n\n    decrypt.Decrypt(nonce, cipherText, tag, decryptedBytes);\n\n    Console.WriteLine(\"Decrypted: {0}\",  Encoding.UTF8.GetString(decryptedBytes));\n}\n```\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Cryptographic algorithms provide many different modes of operation, only some of which provide\nmessage integrity. Without message integrity it could be possible for an adversary to attempt\nto tamper with the ciphertext which could lead to compromising the encryption key. Newer\nalgorithms\napply message integrity to validate ciphertext has not been tampered with.\n\nInstead of using an algorithm that requires configuring a `CipherMode`, an algorithm\nthat has built-in message integrity should be used. If using .NET Framework greater\nthan version 6.0 consider using `ChaCha20Poly1305` or `AES-256-GCM`.\n\nFor older applications, `AES-256-GCM` is recommended, however it has many drawbacks:\n- Slower than `ChaCha20Poly1305`.\n- Catastrophic failure if nonce values are re-used.\n\nExample using `ChaCha20Poly1305`:\n```\n// Generate a random key\nbyte[] key = new byte[32];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(key);\n\nChaCha20Poly1305 encryptor = new ChaCha20Poly1305(key);\n\n// Note nonce values _must_ be regenerated every time they are used.\nvar nonce = new byte[12];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(nonce);\n\nbyte[] plainText = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"Secret text to encrypt\");\nbyte[] cipherText = new byte[plainText.Length];\nvar authTag = new byte[16];\n\nencryptor.Encrypt(nonce, plainText, cipherText, authTag);\nbyte[] output = new byte[cipherText.Length];\nencryptor.Decrypt(nonce, cipherText, authTag, output);\nConsole.WriteLine(\"Output: {0}\", System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(output));\n```\n\nExample using `AES-256-GCM`:\n```\nvar plaintextBytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"Secret text to encrypt\");\nvar key = new byte[32];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(key);\n\nusing var aes = new AesGcm(key);\nvar nonce = new byte[AesGcm.NonceByteSizes.MaxSize];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(nonce);\n\nvar cipherText = new byte[plaintextBytes.Length];\nvar tag = new byte[AesGcm.TagByteSizes.MaxSize];\n\naes.Encrypt(nonce, plaintextBytes, cipherText, tag);\n\n// Decrypt\nusing (var decrypt = new AesGcm(key))\n{\n    var decryptedBytes = new byte[cipherText.Length];\n\n    decrypt.Decrypt(nonce, cipherText, tag, decryptedBytes);\n\n    Console.WriteLine(\"Decrypted: {0}\",  Encoding.UTF8.GetString(decryptedBytes));\n}\n```\n","text":"Cryptographic algorithms provide many different modes of operation, only some of which provide\nmessage integrity. Without message integrity it could be possible for an adversary to attempt\nto tamper with the ciphertext which could lead to compromising the encryption key. Newer\nalgorithms\napply message integrity to validate ciphertext has not been tampered with.\n\nInstead of using an algorithm that requires configuring a `CipherMode`, an algorithm\nthat has built-in message integrity should be used. If using .NET Framework greater\nthan version 6.0 consider using `ChaCha20Poly1305` or `AES-256-GCM`.\n\nFor older applications, `AES-256-GCM` is recommended, however it has many drawbacks:\n- Slower than `ChaCha20Poly1305`.\n- Catastrophic failure if nonce values are re-used.\n\nExample using `ChaCha20Poly1305`:\n```\n// Generate a random key\nbyte[] key = new byte[32];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(key);\n\nChaCha20Poly1305 encryptor = new ChaCha20Poly1305(key);\n\n// Note nonce values _must_ be regenerated every time they are used.\nvar nonce = new byte[12];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(nonce);\n\nbyte[] plainText = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"Secret text to encrypt\");\nbyte[] cipherText = new byte[plainText.Length];\nvar authTag = new byte[16];\n\nencryptor.Encrypt(nonce, plainText, cipherText, authTag);\nbyte[] output = new byte[cipherText.Length];\nencryptor.Decrypt(nonce, cipherText, authTag, output);\nConsole.WriteLine(\"Output: {0}\", System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(output));\n```\n\nExample using `AES-256-GCM`:\n```\nvar plaintextBytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"Secret text to encrypt\");\nvar key = new byte[32];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(key);\n\nusing var aes = new AesGcm(key);\nvar nonce = new byte[AesGcm.NonceByteSizes.MaxSize];\nRandomNumberGenerator.Fill(nonce);\n\nvar cipherText = new byte[plaintextBytes.Length];\nvar tag = new byte[AesGcm.TagByteSizes.MaxSize];\n\naes.Encrypt(nonce, plaintextBytes, cipherText, tag);\n\n// Decrypt\nusing (var decrypt = new AesGcm(key))\n{\n    var decryptedBytes = new byte[cipherText.Length];\n\n    decrypt.Decrypt(nonce, cipherText, tag, decryptedBytes);\n\n    Console.WriteLine(\"Decrypted: {0}\",  Encoding.UTF8.GetString(decryptedBytes));\n}\n```\n"},"id":"AIK_csharp_crypto_WeakCipherMode","name":"AIK_csharp_crypto_WeakCipherMode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_crypto_WeakCipherMode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Deserialization attacks exploit"},"help":{"markdown":"Deserialization attacks exploit","text":"Deserialization attacks exploit"},"id":"AIK_csharp_deserialization_InsecureDeserialization","name":"AIK_csharp_deserialization_InsecureDeserialization","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_deserialization_InsecureDeserialization"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application may allow open redirects if created using user supplied input."},"help":{"markdown":"The application may allow open redirects if created using user supplied input.","text":"The application may allow open redirects if created using user supplied input."},"id":"AIK_csharp_endpoint_rule_UnvalidatedRedirect","name":"AIK_csharp_endpoint_rule_UnvalidatedRedirect","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_endpoint_rule_UnvalidatedRedirect"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"LDAP injection attack possible."},"help":{"markdown":"LDAP injection attack possible.","text":"LDAP injection attack possible."},"id":"AIK_csharp_injection_LdapInjection","name":"AIK_csharp_injection_LdapInjection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_injection_LdapInjection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"XPath injection is a vulnerability that can allow an adversary to inject or modify how an XML\nquery\nis structured. Depending on the logic of the original query, this could lead to adversaries\nextracting unauthorized information or in rare cases bypassing authorization checks.\n\nIt is recommended that LINQ to XML is used instead of XPath for querying XML documents. Care\nmust be taken to **not** call these LINQ functions with user input as they can still lead to\nXPath\ninjection:\n\n- `XPathEvaluate`\n- `XPathSelectElement`\n- `XPathSelectElements`\n\nExample using LINQ to XML to safely extract the first user from a list of users:\n```\n// XDocument is safe from XXE attacks as the resolver is disabled by default\nXDocument doc = XDocument.Load(\"users.xml\");\nXNamespace ns = \"urn:users-schema\";\n\nstring userInput = \"LastName\";\n\n// Get all the users.\nvar user = doc.Descendants(ns + \"user\")\n               .Select(u => new {\n                  FirstName = (string)u.Element(ns + \"first-name\"),\n                  LastName = (string)u.Element(ns + \"last-name\")\n               }).Where(u => u.LastName == userInput).FirstOrDefault();\n\nConsole.WriteLine(user.FirstName + \" \" + user.LastName);\n```\n\nFor more information on LINQ to XML security see:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/linq/linq-xml-security\n\nFor more information on XML security see OWASP's guide:\nhttps://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html#net\n"},"help":{"markdown":"XPath injection is a vulnerability that can allow an adversary to inject or modify how an XML\nquery\nis structured. Depending on the logic of the original query, this could lead to adversaries\nextracting unauthorized information or in rare cases bypassing authorization checks.\n\nIt is recommended that LINQ to XML is used instead of XPath for querying XML documents. Care\nmust be taken to **not** call these LINQ functions with user input as they can still lead to\nXPath\ninjection:\n\n- `XPathEvaluate`\n- `XPathSelectElement`\n- `XPathSelectElements`\n\nExample using LINQ to XML to safely extract the first user from a list of users:\n```\n// XDocument is safe from XXE attacks as the resolver is disabled by default\nXDocument doc = XDocument.Load(\"users.xml\");\nXNamespace ns = \"urn:users-schema\";\n\nstring userInput = \"LastName\";\n\n// Get all the users.\nvar user = doc.Descendants(ns + \"user\")\n               .Select(u => new {\n                  FirstName = (string)u.Element(ns + \"first-name\"),\n                  LastName = (string)u.Element(ns + \"last-name\")\n               }).Where(u => u.LastName == userInput).FirstOrDefault();\n\nConsole.WriteLine(user.FirstName + \" \" + user.LastName);\n```\n\nFor more information on LINQ to XML security see:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/linq/linq-xml-security\n\nFor more information on XML security see OWASP's guide:\nhttps://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html#net\n","text":"XPath injection is a vulnerability that can allow an adversary to inject or modify how an XML\nquery\nis structured. Depending on the logic of the original query, this could lead to adversaries\nextracting unauthorized information or in rare cases bypassing authorization checks.\n\nIt is recommended that LINQ to XML is used instead of XPath for querying XML documents. Care\nmust be taken to **not** call these LINQ functions with user input as they can still lead to\nXPath\ninjection:\n\n- `XPathEvaluate`\n- `XPathSelectElement`\n- `XPathSelectElements`\n\nExample using LINQ to XML to safely extract the first user from a list of users:\n```\n// XDocument is safe from XXE attacks as the resolver is disabled by default\nXDocument doc = XDocument.Load(\"users.xml\");\nXNamespace ns = \"urn:users-schema\";\n\nstring userInput = \"LastName\";\n\n// Get all the users.\nvar user = doc.Descendants(ns + \"user\")\n               .Select(u => new {\n                  FirstName = (string)u.Element(ns + \"first-name\"),\n                  LastName = (string)u.Element(ns + \"last-name\")\n               }).Where(u => u.LastName == userInput).FirstOrDefault();\n\nConsole.WriteLine(user.FirstName + \" \" + user.LastName);\n```\n\nFor more information on LINQ to XML security see:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/linq/linq-xml-security\n\nFor more information on XML security see OWASP's guide:\nhttps://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html#net\n"},"id":"AIK_csharp_injection_XPathInjection","name":"AIK_csharp_injection_XPathInjection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_injection_XPathInjection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The endpoint is potentially accessible to not authorized users."},"help":{"markdown":"The endpoint is potentially accessible to not authorized users.","text":"The endpoint is potentially accessible to not authorized users."},"id":"AIK_csharp_other_AuthorizationBypass","name":"AIK_csharp_other_AuthorizationBypass","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_other_AuthorizationBypass"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"By setting `XsltSettings.EnableScript` to true, an adversary who is able to influence the\nloaded\nXSL document could directly inject code to compromise the system. It is strongly\nrecommended that an alternative approach is used to work with XML data.\n\nFor increased security:\n\n- Never process user-supplied XSL style sheets\n- Ensure `XsltSettings.EnableScript` is set to false\n- Ensure `XsltSettings.EnableDocumentFunction` is set to false\n\nIf the application must calculate values from XML input, instead of using XSL scripts to\nexecute functions, modify the XML document prior to running the\n`XslCompiledTransform.Transform` method.\n\nExample of modifying the XML prior to running `Transform`:\n```\nconst String filename = \"number.xml\";\nconst String stylesheet = \"calc.xsl\";\n\n// Compile the style sheet.\nXsltSettings xslt_settings = new XsltSettings();\nxslt_settings.EnableScript = false; // disable script\nxslt_settings.EnableDocumentFunction = false; // disable document() function\nXslCompiledTransform xslt = new XslCompiledTransform();\nXmlResolver resolver = null; // set a null entity resolver\nxslt.Load(stylesheet, xslt_settings, resolver);\n\n// Load the XML source file, using XDocument for safety\nXDocument doc = XDocument.Load(filename);\n\n// do our modifications to the document before the transformation\n// instead of inside of a script.\ndoc.Element(\"data\").Add(new XElement(\"circle\", new XElement(\"radius\", 12)));\n\n// Create an XmlWriter.\nXmlWriterSettings settings = new XmlWriterSettings();\nsettings.OmitXmlDeclaration = true;\nsettings.Indent = true;\nXmlWriter writer = XmlWriter.Create(\"output.xml\", settings);\n// Finally, execute the transformation.\nxslt.Transform(doc.CreateReader(), writer);\nwriter.Close();\n```\n\nFor more information on security considerations when using XSL see the following URLs:\n- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/data/xml/xslt-security-considerations\n-\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.xml.xsl.xslcompiledtransform?view=net-7.0#security-considerations\n"},"help":{"markdown":"By setting `XsltSettings.EnableScript` to true, an adversary who is able to influence the\nloaded\nXSL document could directly inject code to compromise the system. It is strongly\nrecommended that an alternative approach is used to work with XML data.\n\nFor increased security:\n\n- Never process user-supplied XSL style sheets\n- Ensure `XsltSettings.EnableScript` is set to false\n- Ensure `XsltSettings.EnableDocumentFunction` is set to false\n\nIf the application must calculate values from XML input, instead of using XSL scripts to\nexecute functions, modify the XML document prior to running the\n`XslCompiledTransform.Transform` method.\n\nExample of modifying the XML prior to running `Transform`:\n```\nconst String filename = \"number.xml\";\nconst String stylesheet = \"calc.xsl\";\n\n// Compile the style sheet.\nXsltSettings xslt_settings = new XsltSettings();\nxslt_settings.EnableScript = false; // disable script\nxslt_settings.EnableDocumentFunction = false; // disable document() function\nXslCompiledTransform xslt = new XslCompiledTransform();\nXmlResolver resolver = null; // set a null entity resolver\nxslt.Load(stylesheet, xslt_settings, resolver);\n\n// Load the XML source file, using XDocument for safety\nXDocument doc = XDocument.Load(filename);\n\n// do our modifications to the document before the transformation\n// instead of inside of a script.\ndoc.Element(\"data\").Add(new XElement(\"circle\", new XElement(\"radius\", 12)));\n\n// Create an XmlWriter.\nXmlWriterSettings settings = new XmlWriterSettings();\nsettings.OmitXmlDeclaration = true;\nsettings.Indent = true;\nXmlWriter writer = XmlWriter.Create(\"output.xml\", settings);\n// Finally, execute the transformation.\nxslt.Transform(doc.CreateReader(), writer);\nwriter.Close();\n```\n\nFor more information on security considerations when using XSL see the following URLs:\n- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/data/xml/xslt-security-considerations\n-\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.xml.xsl.xslcompiledtransform?view=net-7.0#security-considerations\n","text":"By setting `XsltSettings.EnableScript` to true, an adversary who is able to influence the\nloaded\nXSL document could directly inject code to compromise the system. It is strongly\nrecommended that an alternative approach is used to work with XML data.\n\nFor increased security:\n\n- Never process user-supplied XSL style sheets\n- Ensure `XsltSettings.EnableScript` is set to false\n- Ensure `XsltSettings.EnableDocumentFunction` is set to false\n\nIf the application must calculate values from XML input, instead of using XSL scripts to\nexecute functions, modify the XML document prior to running the\n`XslCompiledTransform.Transform` method.\n\nExample of modifying the XML prior to running `Transform`:\n```\nconst String filename = \"number.xml\";\nconst String stylesheet = \"calc.xsl\";\n\n// Compile the style sheet.\nXsltSettings xslt_settings = new XsltSettings();\nxslt_settings.EnableScript = false; // disable script\nxslt_settings.EnableDocumentFunction = false; // disable document() function\nXslCompiledTransform xslt = new XslCompiledTransform();\nXmlResolver resolver = null; // set a null entity resolver\nxslt.Load(stylesheet, xslt_settings, resolver);\n\n// Load the XML source file, using XDocument for safety\nXDocument doc = XDocument.Load(filename);\n\n// do our modifications to the document before the transformation\n// instead of inside of a script.\ndoc.Element(\"data\").Add(new XElement(\"circle\", new XElement(\"radius\", 12)));\n\n// Create an XmlWriter.\nXmlWriterSettings settings = new XmlWriterSettings();\nsettings.OmitXmlDeclaration = true;\nsettings.Indent = true;\nXmlWriter writer = XmlWriter.Create(\"output.xml\", settings);\n// Finally, execute the transformation.\nxslt.Transform(doc.CreateReader(), writer);\nwriter.Close();\n```\n\nFor more information on security considerations when using XSL see the following URLs:\n- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/data/xml/xslt-security-considerations\n-\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.xml.xsl.xslcompiledtransform?view=net-7.0#security-considerations\n"},"id":"AIK_csharp_other_UnsafeXSLTSettingUsed","name":"AIK_csharp_other_UnsafeXSLTSettingUsed","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_other_UnsafeXSLTSettingUsed"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application dynamically constructs file or path information. If the path"},"help":{"markdown":"The application dynamically constructs file or path information. If the path","text":"The application dynamically constructs file or path information. If the path"},"id":"AIK_csharp_path_rule_PathTraversal","name":"AIK_csharp_path_rule_PathTraversal","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_path_rule_PathTraversal"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Found usage of MarkupStr function."},"help":{"markdown":"Found usage of MarkupStr function.","text":"Found usage of MarkupStr function."},"id":"AIK_csharp_razor_use_of_markupstr","name":"AIK_csharp_razor_use_of_markupstr","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_razor_use_of_markupstr"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected creation or acceptance of an unsigned JWT"},"help":{"markdown":"Detected creation or acceptance of an unsigned JWT","text":"Detected creation or acceptance of an unsigned JWT"},"id":"AIK_csharp_unsigned_jwt","name":"AIK_csharp_unsigned_jwt","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_unsigned_jwt"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"By using the `[ValidateInput(false)]` attribute in a controller\nclass, the application will disable request validation for that\nmethod. This disables ASP.NET from examining requests for injection\nattacks such as Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS).\n\nIf possible, re-enable validation by using `ValidateInput(true)`.\nIn some cases this may not be possible, in which case ensure how the\nrequest data used is validated and this method does not\noutput user input directly into the view.\n\nFor more information on ASP.NET request validation see OWASP:\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/ASP-NET_Request_Validation\n"},"help":{"markdown":"By using the `[ValidateInput(false)]` attribute in a controller\nclass, the application will disable request validation for that\nmethod. This disables ASP.NET from examining requests for injection\nattacks such as Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS).\n\nIf possible, re-enable validation by using `ValidateInput(true)`.\nIn some cases this may not be possible, in which case ensure how the\nrequest data used is validated and this method does not\noutput user input directly into the view.\n\nFor more information on ASP.NET request validation see OWASP:\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/ASP-NET_Request_Validation\n","text":"By using the `[ValidateInput(false)]` attribute in a controller\nclass, the application will disable request validation for that\nmethod. This disables ASP.NET from examining requests for injection\nattacks such as Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS).\n\nIf possible, re-enable validation by using `ValidateInput(true)`.\nIn some cases this may not be possible, in which case ensure how the\nrequest data used is validated and this method does not\noutput user input directly into the view.\n\nFor more information on ASP.NET request validation see OWASP:\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/ASP-NET_Request_Validation\n"},"id":"AIK_csharp_validation_InputValidation","name":"AIK_csharp_validation_InputValidation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_validation_InputValidation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cross Site Scripting (XSS) is an attack which exploits a web application or system to treat user input as markup or script code."},"help":{"markdown":"Cross Site Scripting (XSS) is an attack which exploits a web application or system to treat user input as markup or script code.","text":"Cross Site Scripting (XSS) is an attack which exploits a web application or system to treat user input as markup or script code."},"id":"AIK_csharp_xss","name":"AIK_csharp_xss","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_xss"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"XXE injection"},"help":{"markdown":"XXE injection","text":"XXE injection"},"id":"AIK_csharp_xxe_injection","name":"AIK_csharp_xxe_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_csharp_xxe_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SSL verification is disabled but should not be (currently CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER= $IS_VERIFIED)"},"help":{"markdown":"SSL verification is disabled but should not be (currently CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER= $IS_VERIFIED)","text":"SSL verification is disabled but should not be (currently CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER= $IS_VERIFIED)"},"id":"AIK_curl-ssl-verifypeer-off","name":"AIK_curl-ssl-verifypeer-off","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_curl-ssl-verifypeer-off"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Accessing Android external storage is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Accessing Android external storage is security-sensitive","text":"Accessing Android external storage is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_dart-external-storage","name":"AIK_dart-external-storage","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_dart-external-storage"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible Command injection"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible Command injection","text":"Possible Command injection"},"id":"AIK_dart_command_injection","name":"AIK_dart_command_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_dart_command_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible SQL injection"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible SQL injection","text":"Possible SQL injection"},"id":"AIK_dart_sqli","name":"AIK_dart_sqli","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_dart_sqli"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Webview debugging is enabled"},"help":{"markdown":"Webview debugging is enabled","text":"Webview debugging is enabled"},"id":"AIK_dart_webview-debug","name":"AIK_dart_webview-debug","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_dart_webview-debug"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"setAllowFileAccess set to true by default"},"help":{"markdown":"setAllowFileAccess set to true by default","text":"setAllowFileAccess set to true by default"},"id":"AIK_dart_webview-loadfile","name":"AIK_dart_webview-loadfile","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_dart_webview-loadfile"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible Path Traversal vulnerability"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible Path Traversal vulnerability","text":"Possible Path Traversal vulnerability"},"id":"AIK_dart_write-as-string","name":"AIK_dart_write-as-string","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_dart_write-as-string"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application uses Doctrine's database functions with potentially user input in the query, which could lead to a SQL injection."},"help":{"markdown":"The application uses Doctrine's database functions with potentially user input in the query, which could lead to a SQL injection.","text":"The application uses Doctrine's database functions with potentially user input in the query, which could lead to a SQL injection."},"id":"AIK_doctrine-orm-sql-injection","name":"AIK_doctrine-orm-sql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_doctrine-orm-sql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Echoing user input risks cross-site scripting vulnerability. You should use htmlentities()."},"help":{"markdown":"Echoing user input risks cross-site scripting vulnerability. You should use htmlentities().","text":"Echoing user input risks cross-site scripting vulnerability. You should use htmlentities()."},"id":"AIK_echoed-request","name":"AIK_echoed-request","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_echoed-request"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The EJS/ECT template has an unescaped variable. Untrusted user input passed to this variable results in Cross Site Scripting (XSS). location."},"help":{"markdown":"The EJS/ECT template has an unescaped variable. Untrusted user input passed to this variable results in Cross Site Scripting (XSS). location.","text":"The EJS/ECT template has an unescaped variable. Untrusted user input passed to this variable results in Cross Site Scripting (XSS). location."},"id":"AIK_ejs_ect_template","name":"AIK_ejs_ect_template","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ejs_ect_template"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Uncontrolled resource consumption because of bad use of String.to_atom"},"help":{"markdown":"Uncontrolled resource consumption because of bad use of String.to_atom","text":"Uncontrolled resource consumption because of bad use of String.to_atom"},"id":"AIK_elixir-atom-exhaustion-string-to-atom","name":"AIK_elixir-atom-exhaustion-string-to-atom","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-atom-exhaustion-string-to-atom"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential Atom Exhaustion Vulnerability Detected"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential Atom Exhaustion Vulnerability Detected","text":"Potential Atom Exhaustion Vulnerability Detected"},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-atom-exhaustion-CVE-2024-31209","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-atom-exhaustion-CVE-2024-31209","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-atom-exhaustion-CVE-2024-31209"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability","text":"Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability"},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-rce-binary-to-term","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-rce-binary-to-term","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-rce-binary-to-term"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability","text":"Potential Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability"},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-rce-code-eval","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-rce-code-eval","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-rce-code-eval"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential SQL injection vulnerability"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential SQL injection vulnerability","text":"Potential SQL injection vulnerability"},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-sql-injection-ectoquery","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-sql-injection-ectoquery","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-sql-injection-ectoquery"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential SQL injection vulnerability. Avoid using forbidden fragment handling methods."},"help":{"markdown":"Potential SQL injection vulnerability. Avoid using forbidden fragment handling methods.","text":"Potential SQL injection vulnerability. Avoid using forbidden fragment handling methods."},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-sql-injection-fragments","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-sql-injection-fragments","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-sql-injection-fragments"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential `Like` injection in Elixir"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential `Like` injection in Elixir","text":"Potential `Like` injection in Elixir"},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-sql-like-injection","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-sql-like-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-sql-like-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Avoid using `raw` with user-generated or unsanitized content. Rendering content with `raw` bypasses HTML escaping, which can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) if any untrusted data is included. Ensure that the input is sanitized or remove `raw` to let Phoenix escape HTML safely."},"help":{"markdown":"Avoid using `raw` with user-generated or unsanitized content. Rendering content with `raw` bypasses HTML escaping, which can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) if any untrusted data is included. Ensure that the input is sanitized or remove `raw` to let Phoenix escape HTML safely.","text":"Avoid using `raw` with user-generated or unsanitized content. Rendering content with `raw` bypasses HTML escaping, which can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) if any untrusted data is included. Ensure that the input is sanitized or remove `raw` to let Phoenix escape HTML safely."},"id":"AIK_elixir-potential-xss-raw","name":"AIK_elixir-potential-xss-raw","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_elixir-potential-xss-raw"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"User controlled data in methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML` or `document.write` is an anti-pattern that can lead to XSS vulnerabilities'"},"help":{"markdown":"User controlled data in methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML` or `document.write` is an anti-pattern that can lead to XSS vulnerabilities'","text":"User controlled data in methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML` or `document.write` is an anti-pattern that can lead to XSS vulnerabilities'"},"id":"AIK_erb_insecure-document-method","name":"AIK_erb_insecure-document-method","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_erb_insecure-document-method"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Evaluating non-constant commands. This can lead to command injection."},"help":{"markdown":"Evaluating non-constant commands. This can lead to command injection.","text":"Evaluating non-constant commands. This can lead to command injection."},"id":"AIK_eval-use","name":"AIK_eval-use","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_eval-use"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The web server executes a command on potential unescaped user input, which may lead to remote command execution."},"help":{"markdown":"The web server executes a command on potential unescaped user input, which may lead to remote command execution.","text":"The web server executes a command on potential unescaped user input, which may lead to remote command execution."},"id":"AIK_exec-use","name":"AIK_exec-use","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_exec-use"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Semgrep found a match"},"help":{"markdown":"Semgrep found a match","text":"Semgrep found a match"},"id":"AIK_express-without-helmet","name":"AIK_express-without-helmet","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_express-without-helmet"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Do not call 'extract()' on user-controllable data. If you must, then you must also provide the EXTR_SKIP flag to prevent overwriting existing variables."},"help":{"markdown":"Do not call 'extract()' on user-controllable data. If you must, then you must also provide the EXTR_SKIP flag to prevent overwriting existing variables.","text":"Do not call 'extract()' on user-controllable data. If you must, then you must also provide the EXTR_SKIP flag to prevent overwriting existing variables."},"id":"AIK_extract-user-data","name":"AIK_extract-user-data","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_extract-user-data"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"FTP allows for unencrypted file transfers. Consider using an encrypted alternative."},"help":{"markdown":"FTP allows for unencrypted file transfers. Consider using an encrypted alternative.","text":"FTP allows for unencrypted file transfers. Consider using an encrypted alternative."},"id":"AIK_ftp-use","name":"AIK_ftp-use","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ftp-use"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"App ignores host keys in SSH connections"},"help":{"markdown":"App ignores host keys in SSH connections","text":"App ignores host keys in SSH connections"},"id":"AIK_go_G106","name":"AIK_go_G106","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_G106"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Url provided to HTTP request as taint input SSRF"},"help":{"markdown":"Url provided to HTTP request as taint input SSRF","text":"Url provided to HTTP request as taint input SSRF"},"id":"AIK_go_G107","name":"AIK_go_G107"