:{"text":"Rendering unescaped input can lead to XSS attacks"},"help":{"markdown":"Rendering unescaped input can lead to XSS attacks","text":"Rendering unescaped input can lead to XSS attacks"},"id":"AIK_go_G203","name":"AIK_go_G203","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_G203"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The web server executes commands on potential user input, which leads to a command injection."},"help":{"markdown":"The web server executes commands on potential user input, which leads to a command injection.","text":"The web server executes commands on potential user input, which leads to a command injection."},"id":"AIK_go_G204","name":"AIK_go_G204","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_G204"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Predictable temp file creation could lead to data exposure"},"help":{"markdown":"Predictable temp file creation could lead to data exposure","text":"Predictable temp file creation could lead to data exposure"},"id":"AIK_go_G303","name":"AIK_go_G303","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_G303"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential file inclusing attack via reading file"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential file inclusing attack via reading file","text":"Potential file inclusing attack via reading file"},"id":"AIK_go_G304","name":"AIK_go_G304","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_G304"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"App might be vulnerable to Zip Slip attack"},"help":{"markdown":"App might be vulnerable to Zip Slip attack","text":"App might be vulnerable to Zip Slip attack"},"id":"AIK_go_G305","name":"AIK_go_G305","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_G305"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected use of unsigned JWT (alg \"none\") or signature-less JWT parsing"},"help":{"markdown":"Detected use of unsigned JWT (alg \"none\") or signature-less JWT parsing","text":"Detected use of unsigned JWT (alg \"none\") or signature-less JWT parsing"},"id":"AIK_go_unsigned_jwt","name":"AIK_go_unsigned_jwt","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_unsigned_jwt"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential XSS in Go"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential XSS in Go","text":"Potential XSS in Go"},"id":"AIK_go_xss","name":"AIK_go_xss","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_go_xss"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected an explicit unescape in a Mustache template, using triple braces '{{{...}}}' or ampersand '&'. If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, ensure no external data can reach this location."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected an explicit unescape in a Mustache template, using triple braces '{{{...}}}' or ampersand '&'. If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, ensure no external data can reach this location.","text":"Detected an explicit unescape in a Mustache template, using triple braces '{{{...}}}' or ampersand '&'. If external data can reach these locations, your application is exposed to a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, ensure no external data can reach this location."},"id":"AIK_handlebar_mustache_template","name":"AIK_handlebar_mustache_template","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_handlebar_mustache_template"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential XSS vulnerability detected."},"help":{"markdown":"Potential XSS vulnerability detected.","text":"Potential XSS vulnerability detected."},"id":"AIK_html_insecure-document-method","name":"AIK_html_insecure-document-method","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_html_insecure-document-method"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"CA pinning missing"},"help":{"markdown":"CA pinning missing","text":"CA pinning missing"},"id":"AIK_ios-ATS-CA-pins","name":"AIK_ios-ATS-CA-pins","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-ATS-CA-pins"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"File loads over http allowed"},"help":{"markdown":"File loads over http allowed","text":"File loads over http allowed"},"id":"AIK_ios-arbitrary-loads","name":"AIK_ios-arbitrary-loads","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-arbitrary-loads"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Perfect Forward security off"},"help":{"markdown":"Perfect Forward security off","text":"Perfect Forward security off"},"id":"AIK_ios-disables-PFS","name":"AIK_ios-disables-PFS","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-disables-PFS"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Media over http allowed"},"help":{"markdown":"Media over http allowed","text":"Media over http allowed"},"id":"AIK_ios-insecure-media-loads","name":"AIK_ios-insecure-media-loads","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-insecure-media-loads"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Webview over http allowed"},"help":{"markdown":"Webview over http allowed","text":"Webview over http allowed"},"id":"AIK_ios-insecure-webview-loads","name":"AIK_ios-insecure-webview-loads","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-insecure-webview-loads"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Local networking allowed"},"help":{"markdown":"Local networking allowed","text":"Local networking allowed"},"id":"AIK_ios-local-networking","name":"AIK_ios-local-networking","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-local-networking"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Minimum TLS version outdated"},"help":{"markdown":"Minimum TLS version outdated","text":"Minimum TLS version outdated"},"id":"AIK_ios-minimum-tls-version","name":"AIK_ios-minimum-tls-version","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_ios-minimum-tls-version"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible active debug code detected."},"help":{"markdown":"Possible active debug code detected.","text":"Possible active debug code detected."},"id":"AIK_java_active-debug-code-printstacktrace","name":"AIK_java_active-debug-code-printstacktrace","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_active-debug-code-printstacktrace"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"CWE-1104"},"help":{"markdown":"CWE-1104","text":"CWE-1104"},"id":"AIK_java_avoid-unmaintained","name":"AIK_java_avoid-unmaintained","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_avoid-unmaintained"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Checks for redefinitions of functions that check TLS/SSL certificate verification. This can lead to vulnerabilities, as simple errors in the code can result in lack of proper certificate validation. This should only be used for debugging purposes because it leads to vulnerability to MTM attacks."},"help":{"markdown":"Checks for redefinitions of functions that check TLS/SSL certificate verification. This can lead to vulnerabilities, as simple errors in the code can result in lack of proper certificate validation. This should only be used for debugging purposes because it leads to vulnerability to MTM attacks.","text":"Checks for redefinitions of functions that check TLS/SSL certificate verification. This can lead to vulnerabilities, as simple errors in the code can result in lack of proper certificate validation. This should only be used for debugging purposes because it leads to vulnerability to MTM attacks."},"id":"AIK_java_bypass-tls-verification","name":"AIK_java_bypass-tls-verification","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_bypass-tls-verification"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted user input in exec() function."},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted user input in exec() function.","text":"Untrusted user input in exec() function."},"id":"AIK_java_command-injection","name":"AIK_java_command-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_command-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The `HttpOnly` attribute when set to `true` protects the cookie value from being accessed by\nclient side JavaScript such\nas reading the `document.cookie` values. By enabling this protection, a website that is\nvulnerable to\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) will be able to block malicious scripts from accessing the cookie\nvalue from JavaScript.\n\nExample of protecting a `Cookie`:\n```\n// Create an HttpOnly cookie.\nCookie someCookie = new Cookie(\"SomeCookieName\", \"SomeValue\");\n// Set HttpOnly flag to true\nsomeCookie.setHttpOnly(true);\n```\n\nFor more information see:\nhttps://jakarta.ee/specifications/servlet/4.0/apidocs/javax/servlet/http/cookie#setHttpOnly-boolean-\n\nSession cookies should be configured with the following security directives:\n\n- [HTTPOnly](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#restrict_access_to_cookies)\n- [Secure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#restrict_access_to_cookies)\n- [SameSite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie/SameSite)\n- [max-agenumber](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Set-Cookie#max-agenumber) : maxAge 0 -> deletes cookie immediately\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The `HttpOnly` attribute when set to `true` protects the cookie value from being accessed by\nclient side JavaScript such\nas reading the `document.cookie` values. By enabling this protection, a website that is\nvulnerable to\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) will be able to block malicious scripts from accessing the cookie\nvalue from JavaScript.\n\nExample of protecting a `Cookie`:\n```\n// Create an HttpOnly cookie.\nCookie someCookie = new Cookie(\"SomeCookieName\", \"SomeValue\");\n// Set HttpOnly flag to true\nsomeCookie.setHttpOnly(true);\n```\n\nFor more information see:\nhttps://jakarta.ee/specifications/servlet/4.0/apidocs/javax/servlet/http/cookie#setHttpOnly-boolean-\n\nSession cookies should be configured with the following security directives:\n\n- [HTTPOnly](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#restrict_access_to_cookies)\n- [Secure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#restrict_access_to_cookies)\n- [SameSite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie/SameSite)\n- [max-agenumber](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Set-Cookie#max-agenumber) : maxAge 0 -> deletes cookie immediately\n","text":"The `HttpOnly` attribute when set to `true` protects the cookie value from being accessed by\nclient side JavaScript such\nas reading the `document.cookie` values. By enabling this protection, a website that is\nvulnerable to\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) will be able to block malicious scripts from accessing the cookie\nvalue from JavaScript.\n\nExample of protecting a `Cookie`:\n```\n// Create an HttpOnly cookie.\nCookie someCookie = new Cookie(\"SomeCookieName\", \"SomeValue\");\n// Set HttpOnly flag to true\nsomeCookie.setHttpOnly(true);\n```\n\nFor more information see:\nhttps://jakarta.ee/specifications/servlet/4.0/apidocs/javax/servlet/http/cookie#setHttpOnly-boolean-\n\nSession cookies should be configured with the following security directives:\n\n- [HTTPOnly](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#restrict_access_to_cookies)\n- [Secure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#restrict_access_to_cookies)\n- [SameSite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie/SameSite)\n- [max-agenumber](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Set-Cookie#max-agenumber) : maxAge 0 -> deletes cookie immediately\n"},"id":"AIK_java_cookie_CookieHTTPOnly","name":"AIK_java_cookie_CookieHTTPOnly","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_cookie_CookieHTTPOnly"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The `org.apache.http.impl.client.DefaultHttpClient` and `javax.net.ssl.SSLContext.getInstance`\nobject instances do not verify the hostnames upon connection.\n\nThis allows for an adversary who is in between the application and the target host to intercept\npotentially sensitive information or transmit malicious data.\n\nDo not use the `org.apache.http.impl.client.DefaultHttpClient();` as it is deprecated. Instead\nuse the new `java.net.http.HttpClient` that was introduced in Java 9.\n\nExample connecting to a host that will automatically do TLS validation:\n```\n// Create a new java.net.http.HttpClient\nHttpClient httpClient = HttpClient.newHttpClient();\n// Create a HttpRequest builder\nHttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()\n        // Create a URI for a website which requires TLS\n        .uri(URI.create(\"https://www.example.com/\"))\n        // Build the request\n        .build();\n\n// Use the httpClient to send the request and use an HttpResponse.BodyHandlers String type\nHttpResponse<String> response = httpClient.send(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString());\n// Debug print\nSystem.out.println(response);\n```\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The `org.apache.http.impl.client.DefaultHttpClient` and `javax.net.ssl.SSLContext.getInstance`\nobject instances do not verify the hostnames upon connection.\n\nThis allows for an adversary who is in between the application and the target host to intercept\npotentially sensitive information or transmit malicious data.\n\nDo not use the `org.apache.http.impl.client.DefaultHttpClient();` as it is deprecated. Instead\nuse the new `java.net.http.HttpClient` that was introduced in Java 9.\n\nExample connecting to a host that will automatically do TLS validation:\n```\n// Create a new java.net.http.HttpClient\nHttpClient httpClient = HttpClient.newHttpClient();\n// Create a HttpRequest builder\nHttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()\n        // Create a URI for a website which requires TLS\n        .uri(URI.create(\"https://www.example.com/\"))\n        // Build the request\n        .build();\n\n// Use the httpClient to send the request and use an HttpResponse.BodyHandlers String type\nHttpResponse<String> response = httpClient.send(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString());\n// Debug print\nSystem.out.println(response);\n```\n","text":"The `org.apache.http.impl.client.DefaultHttpClient` and `javax.net.ssl.SSLContext.getInstance`\nobject instances do not verify the hostnames upon connection.\n\nThis allows for an adversary who is in between the application and the target host to intercept\npotentially sensitive information or transmit malicious data.\n\nDo not use the `org.apache.http.impl.client.DefaultHttpClient();` as it is deprecated. Instead\nuse the new `java.net.http.HttpClient` that was introduced in Java 9.\n\nExample connecting to a host that will automatically do TLS validation:\n```\n// Create a new java.net.http.HttpClient\nHttpClient httpClient = HttpClient.newHttpClient();\n// Create a HttpRequest builder\nHttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()\n        // Create a URI for a website which requires TLS\n        .uri(URI.create(\"https://www.example.com/\"))\n        // Build the request\n        .build();\n\n// Use the httpClient to send the request and use an HttpResponse.BodyHandlers String type\nHttpResponse<String> response = httpClient.send(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString());\n// Debug print\nSystem.out.println(response);\n```\n"},"id":"AIK_java_crypto_WeakTLSProtocol","name":"AIK_java_crypto_WeakTLSProtocol","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_crypto_WeakTLSProtocol"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application was found enabling insecure TLS protocol versions. When enabling protocol\nversions for an `SSLContext`, only the following versions should be allowed:\n- TLSv1.2\n- TLSv1.3\n- DTLSv1.2\n- DTLSv1.3\n\nTo mitigate potential security risks, it is strongly advised to enforce TLS 1.2 as the minimum\nprotocol version and disallow older versions such as TLS 1.0. Do note that newer versions of\nJava do not even support TLS 1.0 and will throw `NoSuchAlgorithmException`. Versions of TLS\nprior to 1.2 could expose the connection to downgrade attacks, where an adversary intercepts\nthe\nconnection and alters the requested protocol version to be a less secure one.\n\nIn many scenarios, relying on the default system configuration does not meet compliance\nstandards. This is due to the application being deployed across diverse systems with varying\nconfigurations and Java versions. While the default value may be secure on modern and\nup-to-date systems, it may not hold true for older systems. Consequently, it is highly\nrecommended to explicitly define a secure configuration in all cases.\n\nExample configuring an SSLContext with TLSv1.2:\n```\n// Create an SSLContext with TLSv1.2 explicitly\nSSLContext tlsContext = SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLSv1.2\"); // or TLSv1.3, DTLSv1.2, DTLSv1.3\n\n// Alternatively, set the enabled protocols\nSSLContext serverSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLS\");\nSSLEngine serverEngine = serverSslContext.createSSLEngine();\n// Calling setEnabledProtocols will override the original context's configured protocol version\nserverEngine.setEnabledProtocols(new String[]{ \"TLSv1.2\" });\n```\n\nFor more information on `SSLContext` see:\n- https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/11/docs/api/java.base/javax/net/ssl/SSLContext.html\n\nFor more information on MiTM attacks see:\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Manipulator-in-the-middle_attack\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The application was found enabling insecure TLS protocol versions. When enabling protocol\nversions for an `SSLContext`, only the following versions should be allowed:\n- TLSv1.2\n- TLSv1.3\n- DTLSv1.2\n- DTLSv1.3\n\nTo mitigate potential security risks, it is strongly advised to enforce TLS 1.2 as the minimum\nprotocol version and disallow older versions such as TLS 1.0. Do note that newer versions of\nJava do not even support TLS 1.0 and will throw `NoSuchAlgorithmException`. Versions of TLS\nprior to 1.2 could expose the connection to downgrade attacks, where an adversary intercepts\nthe\nconnection and alters the requested protocol version to be a less secure one.\n\nIn many scenarios, relying on the default system configuration does not meet compliance\nstandards. This is due to the application being deployed across diverse systems with varying\nconfigurations and Java versions. While the default value may be secure on modern and\nup-to-date systems, it may not hold true for older systems. Consequently, it is highly\nrecommended to explicitly define a secure configuration in all cases.\n\nExample configuring an SSLContext with TLSv1.2:\n```\n// Create an SSLContext with TLSv1.2 explicitly\nSSLContext tlsContext = SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLSv1.2\"); // or TLSv1.3, DTLSv1.2, DTLSv1.3\n\n// Alternatively, set the enabled protocols\nSSLContext serverSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLS\");\nSSLEngine serverEngine = serverSslContext.createSSLEngine();\n// Calling setEnabledProtocols will override the original context's configured protocol version\nserverEngine.setEnabledProtocols(new String[]{ \"TLSv1.2\" });\n```\n\nFor more information on `SSLContext` see:\n- https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/11/docs/api/java.base/javax/net/ssl/SSLContext.html\n\nFor more information on MiTM attacks see:\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Manipulator-in-the-middle_attack\n","text":"The application was found enabling insecure TLS protocol versions. When enabling protocol\nversions for an `SSLContext`, only the following versions should be allowed:\n- TLSv1.2\n- TLSv1.3\n- DTLSv1.2\n- DTLSv1.3\n\nTo mitigate potential security risks, it is strongly advised to enforce TLS 1.2 as the minimum\nprotocol version and disallow older versions such as TLS 1.0. Do note that newer versions of\nJava do not even support TLS 1.0 and will throw `NoSuchAlgorithmException`. Versions of TLS\nprior to 1.2 could expose the connection to downgrade attacks, where an adversary intercepts\nthe\nconnection and alters the requested protocol version to be a less secure one.\n\nIn many scenarios, relying on the default system configuration does not meet compliance\nstandards. This is due to the application being deployed across diverse systems with varying\nconfigurations and Java versions. While the default value may be secure on modern and\nup-to-date systems, it may not hold true for older systems. Consequently, it is highly\nrecommended to explicitly define a secure configuration in all cases.\n\nExample configuring an SSLContext with TLSv1.2:\n```\n// Create an SSLContext with TLSv1.2 explicitly\nSSLContext tlsContext = SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLSv1.2\"); // or TLSv1.3, DTLSv1.2, DTLSv1.3\n\n// Alternatively, set the enabled protocols\nSSLContext serverSslContext = SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLS\");\nSSLEngine serverEngine = serverSslContext.createSSLEngine();\n// Calling setEnabledProtocols will override the original context's configured protocol version\nserverEngine.setEnabledProtocols(new String[]{ \"TLSv1.2\" });\n```\n\nFor more information on `SSLContext` see:\n- https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/11/docs/api/java.base/javax/net/ssl/SSLContext.html\n\nFor more information on MiTM attacks see:\n- https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Manipulator-in-the-middle_attack\n"},"id":"AIK_java_crypto_WeakTLSProtocolVersion","name":"AIK_java_crypto_WeakTLSProtocolVersion","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_crypto_WeakTLSProtocolVersion"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Insecure Cipher Mode detected. See https://owasp.org/www-community/Using_the_Java_Cryptographic_Extensions for more information."},"help":{"markdown":"Insecure Cipher Mode detected. See https://owasp.org/www-community/Using_the_Java_Cryptographic_Extensions for more information.","text":"Insecure Cipher Mode detected. See https://owasp.org/www-community/Using_the_Java_Cryptographic_Extensions for more information."},"id":"AIK_java_crypto_weak-cipher-mode","name":"AIK_java_crypto_weak-cipher-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_crypto_weak-cipher-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of `permitAll()` on 'actuator' endpoint can expose sensitive endpoints to unauthenticated users, bypassing security controls and potentially leading to data leaks, privilege escalation, or full system compromise."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of `permitAll()` on 'actuator' endpoint can expose sensitive endpoints to unauthenticated users, bypassing security controls and potentially leading to data leaks, privilege escalation, or full system compromise.","text":"The use of `permitAll()` on 'actuator' endpoint can expose sensitive endpoints to unauthenticated users, bypassing security controls and potentially leading to data leaks, privilege escalation, or full system compromise."},"id":"AIK_java_exposure_sensitive_endpoints","name":"AIK_java_exposure_sensitive_endpoints","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_exposure_sensitive_endpoints"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected SQL statement that is tainted by user input. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Use parameterized SQL queries or properly sanitize user input instead."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected SQL statement that is tainted by user input. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Use parameterized SQL queries or properly sanitize user input instead.","text":"Detected SQL statement that is tainted by user input. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Use parameterized SQL queries or properly sanitize user input instead."},"id":"AIK_java_formatted-sql-string","name":"AIK_java_formatted-sql-string","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_formatted-sql-string"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a potential path traversal. A malicious actor could control the location of this file, to include going backwards in the directory with '../'. To address this, ensure that user-controlled variables in file paths are sanitized. You may also consider using a utility method such as org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils.getName(...) to only retrieve the file name from the path."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a potential path traversal. A malicious actor could control the location of this file, to include going backwards in the directory with '../'. To address this, ensure that user-controlled variables in file paths are sanitized. You may also consider using a utility method such as org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils.getName(...) to only retrieve the file name from the path.","text":"Detected a potential path traversal. A malicious actor could control the location of this file, to include going backwards in the directory with '../'. To address this, ensure that user-controlled variables in file paths are sanitized. You may also consider using a utility method such as org.apache.commons.io.FilenameUtils.getName(...) to only retrieve the file name from the path."},"id":"AIK_java_httpservlet-path-traversal","name":"AIK_java_httpservlet-path-traversal","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_httpservlet-path-traversal"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application dynamically constructs file or path information. If the path\ninformation comes from user input, it could be abused to read sensitive files,\naccess other users' data, or aid in exploitation to gain further system access.\n\nUser input should never be used in constructing paths or files for interacting\nwith the filesystem. This includes filenames supplied by user uploads or downloads.\nIf possible, consider hashing user input or replacing it with unique values and\nuse `Path.resolve` to resolve and validate the path information\nprior to processing any file functionality.\n\nExample using `Path.resolve` and not allowing direct user input:\n```\n// Class to store our user data along with a randomly generated file name\npublic static class UserData {\n    private String userFileNameUnsafe;\n    private String fileName;\n    public UserData(String userFileName) {\n        this.userFileNameUnsafe = userFileName;\n        // Generate a random ID for the filename\n        this.fileName = UUID.randomUUID().toString();\n    }\n    public String getUserFileNameUnsafe() { return userFileNameUnsafe; };\n    public String getFileName() { return fileName; };\n}\n\npublic static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    // User input, saved only as a reference\n    UserData userData = new UserData(\"..\\\\test.txt\");\n    // Restrict all file processing to this directory only\n    String base = \"/var/app/restricted\";\n    Path basePath = Paths.get(base);\n    // Resolve the full path, but only use our random generated filename\n    Path fullPath = basePath.resolve(userData.getFileName());\n    // verify the path is contained within our basePath\n    if (!fullPath.startsWith(base)) {\n        throw new Exception(\"Invalid path specified!\");\n    }\n    // process / work with file\n}\n```\n\nFor more information on path traversal issues see OWASP:\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Path_Traversal\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The application dynamically constructs file or path information. If the path\ninformation comes from user input, it could be abused to read sensitive files,\naccess other users' data, or aid in exploitation to gain further system access.\n\nUser input should never be used in constructing paths or files for interacting\nwith the filesystem. This includes filenames supplied by user uploads or downloads.\nIf possible, consider hashing user input or replacing it with unique values and\nuse `Path.resolve` to resolve and validate the path information\nprior to processing any file functionality.\n\nExample using `Path.resolve` and not allowing direct user input:\n```\n// Class to store our user data along with a randomly generated file name\npublic static class UserData {\n    private String userFileNameUnsafe;\n    private String fileName;\n    public UserData(String userFileName) {\n        this.userFileNameUnsafe = userFileName;\n        // Generate a random ID for the filename\n        this.fileName = UUID.randomUUID().toString();\n    }\n    public String getUserFileNameUnsafe() { return userFileNameUnsafe; };\n    public String getFileName() { return fileName; };\n}\n\npublic static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    // User input, saved only as a reference\n    UserData userData = new UserData(\"..\\\\test.txt\");\n    // Restrict all file processing to this directory only\n    String base = \"/var/app/restricted\";\n    Path basePath = Paths.get(base);\n    // Resolve the full path, but only use our random generated filename\n    Path fullPath = basePath.resolve(userData.getFileName());\n    // verify the path is contained within our basePath\n    if (!fullPath.startsWith(base)) {\n        throw new Exception(\"Invalid path specified!\");\n    }\n    // process / work with file\n}\n```\n\nFor more information on path traversal issues see OWASP:\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Path_Traversal\n","text":"The application dynamically constructs file or path information. If the path\ninformation comes from user input, it could be abused to read sensitive files,\naccess other users' data, or aid in exploitation to gain further system access.\n\nUser input should never be used in constructing paths or files for interacting\nwith the filesystem. This includes filenames supplied by user uploads or downloads.\nIf possible, consider hashing user input or replacing it with unique values and\nuse `Path.resolve` to resolve and validate the path information\nprior to processing any file functionality.\n\nExample using `Path.resolve` and not allowing direct user input:\n```\n// Class to store our user data along with a randomly generated file name\npublic static class UserData {\n    private String userFileNameUnsafe;\n    private String fileName;\n    public UserData(String userFileName) {\n        this.userFileNameUnsafe = userFileName;\n        // Generate a random ID for the filename\n        this.fileName = UUID.randomUUID().toString();\n    }\n    public String getUserFileNameUnsafe() { return userFileNameUnsafe; };\n    public String getFileName() { return fileName; };\n}\n\npublic static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    // User input, saved only as a reference\n    UserData userData = new UserData(\"..\\\\test.txt\");\n    // Restrict all file processing to this directory only\n    String base = \"/var/app/restricted\";\n    Path basePath = Paths.get(base);\n    // Resolve the full path, but only use our random generated filename\n    Path fullPath = basePath.resolve(userData.getFileName());\n    // verify the path is contained within our basePath\n    if (!fullPath.startsWith(base)) {\n        throw new Exception(\"Invalid path specified!\");\n    }\n    // process / work with file\n}\n```\n\nFor more information on path traversal issues see OWASP:\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Path_Traversal\n"},"id":"AIK_java_inject_rule-SpotbugsPathTraversalAbsolute","name":"AIK_java_inject_rule-SpotbugsPathTraversalAbsolute","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_inject_rule-SpotbugsPathTraversalAbsolute"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"CWE-829"},"help":{"markdown":"CWE-829","text":"CWE-829"},"id":"AIK_java_insecure-url","name":"AIK_java_insecure-url","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_insecure-url"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected use of the 'none' algorithm in a JWT token. The 'none' algorithm assumes the integrity of the token has already been verified. This would allow a malicious actor to forge a JWT token that will automatically be verified. Do not explicitly use the 'none' algorithm. Instead, use an algorithm such as 'HS256'."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected use of the 'none' algorithm in a JWT token. The 'none' algorithm assumes the integrity of the token has already been verified. This would allow a malicious actor to forge a JWT token that will automatically be verified. Do not explicitly use the 'none' algorithm. Instead, use an algorithm such as 'HS256'.","text":"Detected use of the 'none' algorithm in a JWT token. The 'none' algorithm assumes the integrity of the token has already been verified. This would allow a malicious actor to forge a JWT token that will automatically be verified. Do not explicitly use the 'none' algorithm. Instead, use an algorithm such as 'HS256'."},"id":"AIK_java_java-jwt-none-alg","name":"AIK_java_java-jwt-none-alg","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_java-jwt-none-alg"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible JDBC injection detected. Use the parameterized query feature available in queryForObject instead of concatenating or formatting strings: 'jdbc.queryForObject(\"select * from table where name = ?\", Integer.class, parameterName);'"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible JDBC injection detected. Use the parameterized query feature available in queryForObject instead of concatenating or formatting strings: 'jdbc.queryForObject(\"select * from table where name = ?\", Integer.class, parameterName);'","text":"Possible JDBC injection detected. Use the parameterized query feature available in queryForObject instead of concatenating or formatting strings: 'jdbc.queryForObject(\"select * from table where name = ?\", Integer.class, parameterName);'"},"id":"AIK_java_jdbc-sql-formatted-string","name":"AIK_java_jdbc-sql-formatted-string","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_jdbc-sql-formatted-string"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"JSP scriptlet detected. Scriptlets are difficult to use securely and are considered bad practice. See https://stackoverflow.com/a/3180202. Instead, consider migrating to JSF or using the Expression Language '${...}' with the escapeXml function in your JSP files."},"help":{"markdown":"JSP scriptlet detected. Scriptlets are difficult to use securely and are considered bad practice. See https://stackoverflow.com/a/3180202. Instead, consider migrating to JSF or using the Expression Language '${...}' with the escapeXml function in your JSP files.","text":"JSP scriptlet detected. Scriptlets are difficult to use securely and are considered bad practice. See https://stackoverflow.com/a/3180202. Instead, consider migrating to JSF or using the Expression Language '${...}' with the escapeXml function in your JSP files."},"id":"AIK_java_no-scriptlets","name":"AIK_java_no-scriptlets","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_no-scriptlets"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A SQL statement is being concatenated with a potentially user-controllable string, which could lead to a SQL injection vulnerability."},"help":{"markdown":"A SQL statement is being concatenated with a potentially user-controllable string, which could lead to a SQL injection vulnerability.","text":"A SQL statement is being concatenated with a potentially user-controllable string, which could lead to a SQL injection vulnerability."},"id":"AIK_java_no-sql-injection","name":"AIK_java_no-sql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_no-sql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Found object deserialization using ObjectInputStream. Deserializing entire Java objects is dangerous because malicious actors can create Java object streams with unintended consequences. Ensure that the objects being deserialized are not user-controlled. If this must be done, consider using HMACs to sign the data stream to make sure it is not tampered with, or consider only transmitting object fields and populating a new object."},"help":{"markdown":"Found object deserialization using ObjectInputStream. Deserializing entire Java objects is dangerous because malicious actors can create Java object streams with unintended consequences. Ensure that the objects being deserialized are not user-controlled. If this must be done, consider using HMACs to sign the data stream to make sure it is not tampered with, or consider only transmitting object fields and populating a new object.","text":"Found object deserialization using ObjectInputStream. Deserializing entire Java objects is dangerous because malicious actors can create Java object streams with unintended consequences. Ensure that the objects being deserialized are not user-controlled. If this must be done, consider using HMACs to sign the data stream to make sure it is not tampered with, or consider only transmitting object fields and populating a new object."},"id":"AIK_java_object-deserialization","name":"AIK_java_object-deserialization","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_object-deserialization"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application executes an argument using a `ScriptEngine`'s `eval` method. This\nmay allow for direct OS commands to be executed as it's possible to pass in strings\nsuch as `java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec('/bin/sh ...');`.\n\nNever pass user-supplied input directly to the `eval` function. If possible hardcode all\nJavasScript code or use a lookup table to resolve user input to known values. If none of these\ntechniques are possible, use `javax.script.Bindings` to pass input to the script engine.\n\nExample using `Binding` to safely pass in string values:\n```\n// Get ECMAScript engine\nScriptEngine engine = new ScriptEngineManager().getEngineByName(\"ECMAScript\");\n\n// User input, consisting of first and last name\nString userFirstName = \"John\";\nString userLastName = \"Snow\";\n\n// Create bindings to pass into our script, forcing the values to be String.\nBindings bindings = engine.createBindings();\nbindings.put(\"fname\", new String(userFirstName));\nbindings.put(\"lname\", new String(userLastName));\n\n// Example script that concatenates a greeting with the user-supplied input first/last name\nString script = \"var greeting='Hello ';\" +\n// fname and lname variables will be resolved by our bindings defined above\n\"greeting += fname + ' ' + lname;\" +\n// prints greeting\n\"greeting\";\n\ntry {\n  // Execute the script, passing in the bindings\n  Object bindingsResult = engine.eval(script, bindings);\n  // Work with result\n  // ...\n} catch (ScriptException e) {\n  // Handle exception\n  e.printStackTrace();\n}\n```\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The application executes an argument using a `ScriptEngine`'s `eval` method. This\nmay allow for direct OS commands to be executed as it's possible to pass in strings\nsuch as `java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec('/bin/sh ...');`.\n\nNever pass user-supplied input directly to the `eval` function. If possible hardcode all\nJavasScript code or use a lookup table to resolve user input to known values. If none of these\ntechniques are possible, use `javax.script.Bindings` to pass input to the script engine.\n\nExample using `Binding` to safely pass in string values:\n```\n// Get ECMAScript engine\nScriptEngine engine = new ScriptEngineManager().getEngineByName(\"ECMAScript\");\n\n// User input, consisting of first and last name\nString userFirstName = \"John\";\nString userLastName = \"Snow\";\n\n// Create bindings to pass into our script, forcing the values to be String.\nBindings bindings = engine.createBindings();\nbindings.put(\"fname\", new String(userFirstName));\nbindings.put(\"lname\", new String(userLastName));\n\n// Example script that concatenates a greeting with the user-supplied input first/last name\nString script = \"var greeting='Hello ';\" +\n// fname and lname variables will be resolved by our bindings defined above\n\"greeting += fname + ' ' + lname;\" +\n// prints greeting\n\"greeting\";\n\ntry {\n  // Execute the script, passing in the bindings\n  Object bindingsResult = engine.eval(script, bindings);\n  // Work with result\n  // ...\n} catch (ScriptException e) {\n  // Handle exception\n  e.printStackTrace();\n}\n```\n","text":"The application executes an argument using a `ScriptEngine`'s `eval` method. This\nmay allow for direct OS commands to be executed as it's possible to pass in strings\nsuch as `java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec('/bin/sh ...');`.\n\nNever pass user-supplied input directly to the `eval` function. If possible hardcode all\nJavasScript code or use a lookup table to resolve user input to known values. If none of these\ntechniques are possible, use `javax.script.Bindings` to pass input to the script engine.\n\nExample using `Binding` to safely pass in string values:\n```\n// Get ECMAScript engine\nScriptEngine engine = new ScriptEngineManager().getEngineByName(\"ECMAScript\");\n\n// User input, consisting of first and last name\nString userFirstName = \"John\";\nString userLastName = \"Snow\";\n\n// Create bindings to pass into our script, forcing the values to be String.\nBindings bindings = engine.createBindings();\nbindings.put(\"fname\", new String(userFirstName));\nbindings.put(\"lname\", new String(userLastName));\n\n// Example script that concatenates a greeting with the user-supplied input first/last name\nString script = \"var greeting='Hello ';\" +\n// fname and lname variables will be resolved by our bindings defined above\n\"greeting += fname + ' ' + lname;\" +\n// prints greeting\n\"greeting\";\n\ntry {\n  // Execute the script, passing in the bindings\n  Object bindingsResult = engine.eval(script, bindings);\n  // Work with result\n  // ...\n} catch (ScriptException e) {\n  // Handle exception\n  e.printStackTrace();\n}\n```\n"},"id":"AIK_java_script_ScriptInjection","name":"AIK_java_script_ScriptInjection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_script_ScriptInjection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potentially unsanitized user input flows into HTTP response output sinks, which leads to a cross-site scripting attack."},"help":{"markdown":"Potentially unsanitized user input flows into HTTP response output sinks, which leads to a cross-site scripting attack.","text":"Potentially unsanitized user input flows into HTTP response output sinks, which leads to a cross-site scripting attack."},"id":"AIK_java_servletresponse-writer-xss","name":"AIK_java_servletresponse-writer-xss","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_servletresponse-writer-xss"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible Spring Expression Language (SpEL) Injection"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible Spring Expression Language (SpEL) Injection","text":"Possible Spring Expression Language (SpEL) Injection"},"id":"AIK_java_spel_injection","name":"AIK_java_spel_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_spel_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"CSRF protection is disabled for this configuration. This is a security risk."},"help":{"markdown":"CSRF protection is disabled for this configuration. This is a security risk.","text":"CSRF protection is disabled for this configuration. This is a security risk."},"id":"AIK_java_spring-csrf-disabled","name":"AIK_java_spring-csrf-disabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_spring-csrf-disabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The org.springframework:spring-web package is vulnerable to deserialization of untrusted data leading to Remote Code Execution (RCE). The readRemoteInvocation method in HttpInvokerServiceExporter.class does not properly verify or restrict untrusted objects prior to deserializing them. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending malicious requests containing crafted objects, which when deserialized, execute arbitrary code on the vulnerable system."},"help":{"markdown":"The org.springframework:spring-web package is vulnerable to deserialization of untrusted data leading to Remote Code Execution (RCE). The readRemoteInvocation method in HttpInvokerServiceExporter.class does not properly verify or restrict untrusted objects prior to deserializing them. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending malicious requests containing crafted objects, which when deserialized, execute arbitrary code on the vulnerable system.","text":"The org.springframework:spring-web package is vulnerable to deserialization of untrusted data leading to Remote Code Execution (RCE). The readRemoteInvocation method in HttpInvokerServiceExporter.class does not properly verify or restrict untrusted objects prior to deserializing them. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending malicious requests containing crafted objects, which when deserialized, execute arbitrary code on the vulnerable system."},"id":"AIK_java_spring-http-invoker-service-exposed","name":"AIK_java_spring-http-invoker-service-exposed","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_spring-http-invoker-service-exposed"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"To ensure security, the Initialization Vector (IV) must be both random and unique. Avoid hard-coded, static IVs. Instead, generate a fresh, cryptographically random IV for each operation using the SecureRandom class."},"help":{"markdown":"To ensure security, the Initialization Vector (IV) must be both random and unique. Avoid hard-coded, static IVs. Instead, generate a fresh, cryptographically random IV for each operation using the SecureRandom class.","text":"To ensure security, the Initialization Vector (IV) must be both random and unique. Avoid hard-coded, static IVs. Instead, generate a fresh, cryptographically random IV for each operation using the SecureRandom class."},"id":"AIK_java_static_IV_generation","name":"AIK_java_static_IV_generation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_static_IV_generation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input might be used to build an HTTP request"},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input might be used to build an HTTP request","text":"Untrusted input might be used to build an HTTP request"},"id":"AIK_java_tainted-ssrf-spring-add","name":"AIK_java_tainted-ssrf-spring-add","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_tainted-ssrf-spring-add"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected use of unsigned jwt token"},"help":{"markdown":"Detected use of unsigned jwt token","text":"Detected use of unsigned jwt token"},"id":"AIK_java_unsigned_jwt","name":"AIK_java_unsigned_jwt","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_unsigned_jwt"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"XMLDecoder should not be used to parse untrusted data. Deserializing user input can lead to arbitrary code execution. Use an alternative and explicitly disable external entities. See https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html for alternatives and vulnerability prevention."},"help":{"markdown":"XMLDecoder should not be used to parse untrusted data. Deserializing user input can lead to arbitrary code execution. Use an alternative and explicitly disable external entities. See https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html for alternatives and vulnerability prevention.","text":"XMLDecoder should not be used to parse untrusted data. Deserializing user input can lead to arbitrary code execution. Use an alternative and explicitly disable external entities. See https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html for alternatives and vulnerability prevention."},"id":"AIK_java_xml-decoder","name":"AIK_java_xml-decoder","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_xml-decoder"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application performs XSLT translation with potentially malicious input. An adversary who is able to influence the loaded XSL document could call XSL functions.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"The application performs XSLT translation with potentially malicious input. An adversary who is able to influence the loaded XSL document could call XSL functions.\n","text":"The application performs XSLT translation with potentially malicious input. An adversary who is able to influence the loaded XSL document could call XSL functions.\n"},"id":"AIK_java_xml_XsltTransform","name":"AIK_java_xml_XsltTransform","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_xml_XsltTransform"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"XML external entities are enabled for this XMLInputFactory. This is vulnerable to XML external entity attacks. Disable external entities by setting \"javax.xml.stream.isSupportingExternalEntities\" to false."},"help":{"markdown":"XML external entities are enabled for this XMLInputFactory. This is vulnerable to XML external entity attacks. Disable external entities by setting \"javax.xml.stream.isSupportingExternalEntities\" to false.","text":"XML external entities are enabled for this XMLInputFactory. This is vulnerable to XML external entity attacks. Disable external entities by setting \"javax.xml.stream.isSupportingExternalEntities\" to false."},"id":"AIK_java_xmlinputfactory-external-entities-enabled","name":"AIK_java_xmlinputfactory-external-entities-enabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_xmlinputfactory-external-entities-enabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible XPath injection"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible XPath injection","text":"Possible XPath injection"},"id":"AIK_java_xpath_injection","name":"AIK_java_xpath_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_xpath_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Unsafe XML parsing can lead to XML External Entity (XXE) attacks, which may result in data exposure, denial of service, or server-side request forgery (SSRF)."},"help":{"markdown":"Unsafe XML parsing can lead to XML External Entity (XXE) attacks, which may result in data exposure, denial of service, or server-side request forgery (SSRF).","text":"Unsafe XML parsing can lead to XML External Entity (XXE) attacks, which may result in data exposure, denial of service, or server-side request forgery (SSRF)."},"id":"AIK_java_xxe_documentbuilder_factory","name":"AIK_java_xxe_documentbuilder_factory","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_java_xxe_documentbuilder_factory"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Dynamic data ($VAR) is passed to a jQuery DOM insertion sink without sanitization. If this data originates from user input, a database, or an API response, an attacker can inject arbitrary HTML/JS."},"help":{"markdown":"Dynamic data ($VAR) is passed to a jQuery DOM insertion sink without sanitization. If this data originates from user input, a database, or an API response, an attacker can inject arbitrary HTML/JS.","text":"Dynamic data ($VAR) is passed to a jQuery DOM insertion sink without sanitization. If this data originates from user input, a database, or an API response, an attacker can inject arbitrary HTML/JS."},"id":"AIK_jquery-cdn-xss","name":"AIK_jquery-cdn-xss","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_jquery-cdn-xss"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible DOM XSS vulnerability"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible DOM XSS vulnerability","text":"Possible DOM XSS vulnerability"},"id":"AIK_jquery-insecure-method","name":"AIK_jquery-insecure-method","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_jquery-insecure-method"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Calling this method with untrusted user data exposes your application to XSS security risks"},"help":{"markdown":"Calling this method with untrusted user data exposes your application to XSS security risks","text":"Calling this method with untrusted user data exposes your application to XSS security risks"},"id":"AIK_js-bypass-security-trust-url","name":"AIK_js-bypass-security-trust-url","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js-bypass-security-trust-url"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible Path Traversal"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible Path Traversal","text":"Possible Path Traversal"},"id":"AIK_js-path-traversal-sendFile","name":"AIK_js-path-traversal-sendFile","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js-path-traversal-sendFile"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Potential XSS vulnerability"},"help":{"markdown":"Potential XSS vulnerability","text":"Potential XSS vulnerability"},"id":"AIK_js_insecure-document-method","name":"AIK_js_insecure-document-method","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_insecure-document-method"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Insecure WebSocket connection detected"},"help":{"markdown":"Insecure WebSocket connection detected","text":"Insecure WebSocket connection detected"},"id":"AIK_js_insecure_transport_websockets","name":"AIK_js_insecure_transport_websockets","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_insecure_transport_websockets"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"JWT signature not verified"},"help":{"markdown":"JWT signature not verified","text":"JWT signature not verified"},"id":"AIK_js_jwt_unsafe_decode","name":"AIK_js_jwt_unsafe_decode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_jwt_unsafe_decode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possible LDAP injection"},"help":{"markdown":"Possible LDAP injection","text":"Possible LDAP injection"},"id":"AIK_js_ldap_injection","name":"AIK_js_ldap_injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_ldap_injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected use of parseXml() function with the `noent` field set to `true`. This can lead to an XML External Entities (XXE) attack if untrusted data is passed into it."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected use of parseXml() function with the `noent` field set to `true`. This can lead to an XML External Entities (XXE) attack if untrusted data is passed into it.","text":"Detected use of parseXml() function with the `noent` field set to `true`. This can lead to an XML External Entities (XXE) attack if untrusted data is passed into it."},"id":"AIK_js_noent-libxml","name":"AIK_js_noent-libxml","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_noent-libxml"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Prototype Pollution via recursive function call"},"help":{"markdown":"Prototype Pollution via recursive function call","text":"Prototype Pollution via recursive function call"},"id":"AIK_js_prototype_pollution_recursive_func_call","name":"AIK_js_prototype_pollution_recursive_func_call","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_prototype_pollution_recursive_func_call"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input might be injected into a command executed by the application, resulting in a command injection vulnerability. This enables an attacker to execute arbitrary commands, potentially taking complete control of the system. To prevent this, avoid executing OS commands with user input. If unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe methods for executing the commands."},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input might be injected into a command executed by the application, resulting in a command injection vulnerability. This enables an attacker to execute arbitrary commands, potentially taking complete control of the system. To prevent this, avoid executing OS commands with user input. If unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe methods for executing the commands.","text":"Untrusted input might be injected into a command executed by the application, resulting in a command injection vulnerability. This enables an attacker to execute arbitrary commands, potentially taking complete control of the system. To prevent this, avoid executing OS commands with user input. If unavoidable, validate and sanitize the input, and use safe methods for executing the commands."},"id":"AIK_js_shell_injection_child_process","name":"AIK_js_shell_injection_child_process","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_shell_injection_child_process"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Exposing `process.env` via Vite `define` can leak server-side environment variables to client-side bundles."},"help":{"markdown":"Exposing `process.env` via Vite `define` can leak server-side environment variables to client-side bundles.","text":"Exposing `process.env` via Vite `define` can leak server-side environment variables to client-side bundles."},"id":"AIK_js_ssr_process_env_exposure","name":"AIK_js_ssr_process_env_exposure","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_ssr_process_env_exposure"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Tainted var $URL in $LIB call SSRF"},"help":{"markdown":"Tainted var $URL in $LIB call SSRF","text":"Tainted var $URL in $LIB call SSRF"},"id":"AIK_js_ssrf","name":"AIK_js_ssrf","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_ssrf"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Direct use of user-controlled objects as arguments to the express.render() function can result in server-side template injection when the template engine evaluates untrusted data."},"help":{"markdown":"Direct use of user-controlled objects as arguments to the express.render() function can result in server-side template injection when the template engine evaluates untrusted data.","text":"Direct use of user-controlled objects as arguments to the express.render() function can result in server-side template injection when the template engine evaluates untrusted data."},"id":"AIK_js_tainted_express_render","name":"AIK_js_tainted_express_render","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_tainted_express_render"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"LoadEnv with the third parameter set to '' can leak sensitive data"},"help":{"markdown":"LoadEnv with the third parameter set to '' can leak sensitive data","text":"LoadEnv with the third parameter set to '' can leak sensitive data"},"id":"AIK_js_vite_env_leakage","name":"AIK_js_vite_env_leakage","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_vite_env_leakage"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Use of window.location.href can lead to open-redirect if user input is used for redirection."},"help":{"markdown":"Use of window.location.href can lead to open-redirect if user input is used for redirection.","text":"Use of window.location.href can lead to open-redirect if user input is used for redirection."},"id":"AIK_js_xss_location","name":"AIK_js_xss_location","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_js_xss_location"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"xss in jsp"},"help":{"markdown":"xss in jsp","text":"xss in jsp"},"id":"AIK_jsp_xss","name":"AIK_jsp_xss","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_jsp_xss"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Accessing Android external storage is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Accessing Android external storage is security-sensitive","text":"Accessing Android external storage is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_android-external-storage","name":"AIK_kotlin_android-external-storage","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_android-external-storage"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Using biometric authentication without a cryptographic solution is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Using biometric authentication without a cryptographic solution is security-sensitive","text":"Using biometric authentication without a cryptographic solution is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_biometric-without-crypto","name":"AIK_kotlin_biometric-without-crypto","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_biometric-without-crypto"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Broadcasting intents is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Broadcasting intents is security-sensitive","text":"Broadcasting intents is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_broadcast-intents","name":"AIK_kotlin_broadcast-intents","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_broadcast-intents"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Handling user-controlled data into java.lang.Runtime calls can lead to command injection"},"help":{"markdown":"Handling user-controlled data into java.lang.Runtime calls can lead to command injection","text":"Handling user-controlled data into java.lang.Runtime calls can lead to command injection"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_command_injection_runtime","name":"AIK_kotlin_command_injection_runtime","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_command_injection_runtime"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An XML External Entity (XXE) injection attack exploits weakly configured XML parsers that process untrusted input. By injecting malicious Document Type Definitions (DTDs), an attacker can access sensitive files on the server's filesystem, exfiltrate data, or make unauthorized external requests. This can also lead to a denial-of-service condition by exhausting system resources through entity expansion."},"help":{"markdown":"An XML External Entity (XXE) injection attack exploits weakly configured XML parsers that process untrusted input. By injecting malicious Document Type Definitions (DTDs), an attacker can access sensitive files on the server's filesystem, exfiltrate data, or make unauthorized external requests. This can also lead to a denial-of-service condition by exhausting system resources through entity expansion.","text":"An XML External Entity (XXE) injection attack exploits weakly configured XML parsers that process untrusted input. By injecting malicious Document Type Definitions (DTDs), an attacker can access sensitive files on the server's filesystem, exfiltrate data, or make unauthorized external requests. This can also lead to a denial-of-service condition by exhausting system resources through entity expansion."},"id":"AIK_kotlin_factory_xxe","name":"AIK_kotlin_factory_xxe","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_factory_xxe"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Authorizing non-authenticated users to use keys in the Android KeyStore is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Authorizing non-authenticated users to use keys in the Android KeyStore is security-sensitive","text":"Authorizing non-authenticated users to use keys in the Android KeyStore is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_keystore-non-auth","name":"AIK_kotlin_keystore-non-auth","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_keystore-non-auth"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Receiving intents is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Receiving intents is security-sensitive","text":"Receiving intents is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_receive-intents","name":"AIK_kotlin_receive-intents","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_receive-intents"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a formatted string in a SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Use a prepared statements instead."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a formatted string in a SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Use a prepared statements instead.","text":"Detected a formatted string in a SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Use a prepared statements instead."},"id":"AIK_kotlin_sqli","name":"AIK_kotlin_sqli","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_sqli"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected use of unsigned/insecure jwt token"},"help":{"markdown":"Detected use of unsigned/insecure jwt token","text":"Detected use of unsigned/insecure jwt token"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_unsigned_jwt","name":"AIK_kotlin_unsigned_jwt","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_unsigned_jwt"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Delivering code in production with debug features activated is security-sensitive."},"help":{"markdown":"Delivering code in production with debug features activated is security-sensitive.","text":"Delivering code in production with debug features activated is security-sensitive."},"id":"AIK_kotlin_webview-debug","name":"AIK_kotlin_webview-debug","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_webview-debug"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Enabling file access for WebViews is security-sensitive"},"help":{"markdown":"Enabling file access for WebViews is security-sensitive","text":"Enabling file access for WebViews is security-sensitive"},"id":"AIK_kotlin_webview-file-access","name":"AIK_kotlin_webview-file-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_webview-file-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Enabling universal access from the file:// scheme is unsafe. It allows origins in the file:// scheme to access content from any origin (including web origins)."},"help":{"markdown":"Enabling universal access from the file:// scheme is unsafe. It allows origins in the file:// scheme to access content from any origin (including web origins).","text":"Enabling universal access from the file:// scheme is unsafe. It allows origins in the file:// scheme to access content from any origin (including web origins)."},"id":"AIK_kotlin_webview-file-access-universal","name":"AIK_kotlin_webview-file-access-universal","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_webview-file-access-universal"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Enabling JavaScript support for WebViews is security-sensitive."},"help":{"markdown":"Enabling JavaScript support for WebViews is security-sensitive.","text":"Enabling JavaScript support for WebViews is security-sensitive."},"id":"AIK_kotlin_webview-js","name":"AIK_kotlin_webview-js","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_kotlin_webview-js"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Found a configuration file where the secure attribute is not set to 'true'. Setting 'secure' to 'true' prevents the client from transmitting the cookie over unencrypted channels and therefore prevents cookies from being stolen through man in the middle attacks. "},"help":{"markdown":"Found a configuration file where the secure attribute is not set to 'true'. Setting 'secure' to 'true' prevents the client from transmitting the cookie over unencrypted channels and therefore prevents cookies from being stolen through man in the middle attacks. ","text":"Found a configuration file where the secure attribute is not set to 'true'. Setting 'secure' to 'true' prevents the client from transmitting the cookie over unencrypted channels and therefore prevents cookies from being stolen through man in the middle attacks. "},"id":"AIK_laravel-cookie-secure-set","name":"AIK_laravel-cookie-secure-set","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_laravel-cookie-secure-set"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a SQL query based on user input."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a SQL query based on user input.","text":"Detected a SQL query based on user input."},"id":"AIK_laravel-sql-injection","name":"AIK_laravel-sql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_laravel-sql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An object is created using permit!, which overrides the default mass assignment protection and potentially allows an user to change fields they shouldn't be allowed to change."},"help":{"markdown":"An object is created using permit!, which overrides the default mass assignment protection and potentially allows an user to change fields they shouldn't be allowed to change.","text":"An object is created using permit!, which overrides the default mass assignment protection and potentially allows an user to change fields they shouldn't be allowed to change."},"id":"AIK_mass-assignment","name":"AIK_mass-assignment","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_mass-assignment"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"If \"most_recent\" is set to \"true\" without restricting results by owner or image ID, there is a risk that an unintended image from an untrusted source could be selected. To prevent this, ensure that the query includes an \"owners\" field or appropriate filters to control the selection criteria.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"If \"most_recent\" is set to \"true\" without restricting results by owner or image ID, there is a risk that an unintended image from an untrusted source could be selected. To prevent this, ensure that the query includes an \"owners\" field or appropriate filters to control the selection criteria.\n","text":"If \"most_recent\" is set to \"true\" without restricting results by owner or image ID, there is a risk that an unintended image from an untrusted source could be selected. To prevent this, ensure that the query includes an \"owners\" field or appropriate filters to control the selection criteria.\n"},"id":"AIK_missing_owner_reference_in_AMI","name":"AIK_missing_owner_reference_in_AMI","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":[]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: AIK_missing_owner_reference_in_AMI"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Error messages with stack traces can expose sensitive information about the application."},"help":{"markdown":"Error messages with stack traces can expose sensitive information about the application.","text":"Error messages with stack traces can expose sensitive information about the application."},"id":"AIK_node_error_send","name":"AIK_node_error_send","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":